from pathlib import Path
import subprocess,json,hashlib
p=Path('.tmp/deployment-integration-review');head=subprocess.run(['git','rev-parse','HEAD'],capture_output=True,text=True,check=True).stdout.strip()
if head!='d61725c579428c324e0037720eb33c631d086c8f':raise ValueError('HEAD changed')
for mode in ['normal','optimized']:
 r=json.loads((p/('chain-'+mode+'.json')).read_text())
 if r['events']!=['DeployIntent','DeployReceipt','Observation','Observation','SmokePassed'] or r['post_calls']!=1 or r['get_preceding_remote_events']!=['DeployReceipt','Observation'] or not r['identity_preserved'] or not r['raw_smoke_preserved']:raise ValueError(mode)
paths=subprocess.run(['git','diff','--name-only','origin/main...HEAD','--','tools/site'],capture_output=True,text=True,check=True).stdout.splitlines()
for name in paths:
 f=p/'source'/name;f.parent.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True);f.write_bytes(Path(name).read_bytes())
report='''# Independent deployment integration review

Scope: d61725c579428c324e0037720eb33c631d086c8f, compared with origin/main bd74af3. Reviewed deployment adapters, integration tests, README scope and spec15 contracts. No implementation edits or live API/publication operations.

No remaining blocking finding in the integrated adapter scope. All 19 changed Python implementation/test files (excluding the empty package marker) match individually sealed reviewed source, allowing only CRLF/LF normalization. The older receipt snapshot has CRLF; this is not a semantic source change. Validated all indexed size/hash entries of the 9 directly relevant review seals (162 files). The merge commit has no tree difference from its first parent.

Independently ran a real-bare-Git end-to-end connection normally and under python -O: one fake creation response, pending and succeeded fake status responses, then a fake public byte-smoke report. Remote journal order was DeployIntent, DeployReceipt, Observation, Observation, SmokePassed. Each GET saw its required prior remote record; transaction and canonical payload digest remained identical; the original smoke report survived remote storage. The optimized run's recorded outcomes were independently checked outside optimized Python. This complements prior failure/boundary tests without repeating every archive fixture.

Confirmed the known fixes remain present: Receipt invariant validation, strict HTTP length/framing, process-bounded transport, deadline coverage of initial journal reading and persistence, no polling after unknown creation, one POST after durable remote intent, and the smoke-specific 300-second observation deadline separate from the longer transaction budget. Existing review seals retain the initial counterexamples and fixed reruns. Snapshot matching and seal results are in prior-source-match.json and prior-seal-validation.json.

Caller-owned publisher eligibility, lock, remote protection, artifact provenance, reconcile and total remaining budget are still necessary. API success and byte smoke remain evidence rather than current deployment identity/LKG authorization. Release verification checks immutable metadata and downloaded pins; recover additionally verifies the original tar, but neither authorizes rollback. The new chain uses fake API/HTTP responses and real local Git; TLS, actual Pages/publication, complete publisher workflow, recovery orchestration and LKG promotion were not tested. Parent full-suite/repository runs are separate evidence, not independently claimed here.

An initial scratch matching attempt stopped on the CRLF-only receipt difference; it was not a production/test failure. Matching was then explicitly normalized for line endings while each preserved snapshot was verified against its own exact-byte seal.
'''
(p/'review.md').write_text(report,encoding='utf8',newline='\n')
rows=[]
for f in sorted(p.rglob('*')):
 if f.is_file() and f.name!='manifest.json':
  b=f.read_bytes();rows.append(dict(path=f.relative_to(p).as_posix(),bytes=len(b),sha256=hashlib.sha256(b).hexdigest()))
(p/'manifest.json').write_text(json.dumps(dict(source_commit=head,files=rows),indent=2)+'\n',encoding='utf8');print(len(rows),sum(r['bytes'] for r in rows))
